<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Keeps the two cloud nodes in step with this laptop, every ten minutes.

       Before this existed, both directions relied on somebody remembering.
       On 2026-09-05 both were wrong at once and neither said so: the display
       node had been serving a day-old set of marks because publishing a
       snapshot only ever happened inside daily.sh (which had not run), and
       origin/main was three days behind because a push that everyone believed
       had happened never landed. Every dashboard looked healthy throughout.

       So the interval is not the point — the reporting is. The script pushes
       only what changed, gates code on the same test suite the cloud updater
       runs before it swaps images, verifies with the remote that the push
       actually landed, and sends a Lark DM when a leg is stuck.

       PATH is set explicitly: launchd starts with almost none, and both git
       (credential helper) and lark-cli (notifications) live outside it. -->
  <key>Label</key><string>com.ideagen40.cloudsync</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.12/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/yuesongcai/IdeaGen40/scripts/sync_to_cloud.py</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/yuesongcai/IdeaGen40</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>600</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/yuesongcai/IdeaGen40/data/logs/cloud_sync.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/yuesongcai/IdeaGen40/data/logs/cloud_sync.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
